  "period_note": "Balance sheet is the period-end snapshot (reported) as at 31 March 2025, from Midland Bank's own genuinely-filed, BSEC/DSE/CSE-submitted quarterly financial statements (Un-Audited). Income-statement items are CUMULATIVE from 1 January 2025 (1 January to 31 March 2025), flagged via the _cumulative suffix. SOLO / STANDALONE basis -- 'Midland Bank PLC.' / 'Midland Bank Limited' single-entity statements, distinct from the Consolidated statements the bank has also prepared since Q1 2024 (covering its subsidiary Midland Bank Asset Management Company Ltd., BSEC-licensed 4 August 2024); this file uses only the Solo figures, matching the bank's main annual Q4 series basis. provision_charge_cumulative and tax_expense_cumulative are the report's own printed 'Total Provision' and 'Provision for Tax' lines (reported, not calculated, unlike the annual Q4 series which has to derive these because its summary table omits them). NAV per share of 15.29 is not printed on this quarter's own Solo balance sheet page but is taken from the FY2025 annual report's 'Evaluation of Quarterly Financials' table (31-Mar-25 column) and independently confirmed by calculation (9,777,405,184 / 639,669,753 shares = 15.29). This record supersedes an earlier version of this file in the same working session that was built solely from the FY2025 annual report's summary table; every figure below has now been independently verified against this bank's own primary quarterly filing and the figures match to the taka (net_interest_income_cumulative, investment_income totals, operating_profit_cumulative, provision, PBT, tax, PAT, EPS, and NOCFPS all reproduce exactly). Also independently reproduced in the Q1-2026 filing's comparative column.",
